According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global grain mill product market was valued at USD 3.6 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 6.0 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 5.8% during the forecast period (2026–2034). This growth is driven by a confluence of consumer health trends, the modernization of agro processing facilities in emerging economies, and relentless innovation from leading equipment manufacturers.
Grain mill products comprise equipment such as stone mills, hammer mills and roller mills that reduce cereals into flour or meal for human consumption and animal feed. These machines are integral to bakery chains, packaged food manufacturers and small scale artisanal producers because they determine particle size, nutritional retention and processing efficiency.
